      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"They will whisper words like 'inflation' and 'isolation'; the predictable rebuttals of those benefiting from the status quo. They claim higher costs, but I ask you, what is the cost of a national treasury hollowed out, or a workforce rendered obsolete by phantom global demands? Their perceived 'stability' is merely the quiet rot of dependency; a fever that starves the body in the name of cheap temporary comfort. We choose the discipline of self-reliance over the anesthesia of false affordability.\"",
      "source": "target",
